2. In this Notification, unless the context otherwise requires —
“covered pedestrian linkway” means a walkway on the ground which —
(a)is covered on the top;
(b)is open on all sides;
(c)is connected to or facilitates pedestrian access to any public transport facility, public facility or building; and
(d)is not part of any building;
“Town Council” means a Town Council established under section 4 of the Town Councils Act (Cap. 329A).

3.—(1) Subject to paragraphs 4 and 5 and any other written law, the following operations involving the development of land, carried out by any statutory authority, are authorised under section 21(6) of the Act:
(a)the construction of a covered pedestrian linkway which is not within the boundaries of a street;
(b)the carrying out of works for the maintenance or improvement of a covered pedestrian linkway which is not within the boundaries of a street.
(2) Subject to paragraphs 4 and 5 and any other written law, the following operations involving the development of land, carried out by any Town Council, are authorised under section 21(6) of the Act:
(a)the construction of a covered pedestrian linkway;
(b)the carrying out of works for the maintenance or improvement of a covered pedestrian linkway.

4. The authorisation for carrying out an operation involving the development of land under paragraph 3 shall apply subject to the following conditions:
(a)the written consent of the owner of the land for the carrying out of the operation is obtained prior to the carrying out of the operation;
(b)any approval from any relevant authority required for the carrying out of the operation is obtained prior to the carrying out of the operation;
(c)no part of the operation comprises works that are not authorised under the Act.
